mains:{angles:['How far did the **1935 Act** shape the Constitution, both in structure (federation, lists, emergency, Governor) and in spirit (a strong Centre)?','Continuity vs. change: the Constitution as a **break** with colonial rule (sovereignty, adult franchise, FRs) yet a **continuation** of its administrative apparatus (IAS, district administration, Art 356 echoing Sec 93).','Separate electorates and the politics of representation, from 1909 to the Poona Pact and the reserved seats of Arts 330–332.'],judgments:[],committees:['**Lee Commission (1923–24)** — Public Service Commission','**Simon Commission (1927)**','**Nehru Report (1928)** — first Indian draft constitution; a list of fundamental rights; dominion status'],quotes:['Nehru called the 1935 Act "a machine with strong brakes but no engine".']},
